JH schrieb:
> 
> I just started playing healers.  Would you recommend to quaff all the
> !oHealing and extra healing at the beginning, or am I better off saving them
> for a tight spot?

Somewhere in between: my rule of thumb is to keep one potion of extra
healing, two of healing. This way, i have about 20 hitpoints from the
start and have a few potions left in case i get hurt badly and don't
want to risk failing a healing spell. Also, healing potions will cure
blindness, which can be helpful when encountering yellow lights.

> Any other general healer survivability recommendations would be appreciated

Being able to cast your healing spells is valuable - only use metallic
body armour if this gives you a _big_ AC bonus: being able to heal
yourself and your pet is the one big asset you have in the early game.
Pick up any sort of weapon and spell-friendly armour you can find;
getting some daggers as throwing weapons is a good idea, as is keeping
your pet alife (hoping that it takes out the more troublesome monsters
until you can start to fight things yourself).

Open and close doors and push boulders as much as you can - this
exercises your strength.

